.TH WELLHW 1 "August 2026" "wellhw 1.3" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
wellhw \- hardware report (CPU, GPU, board, RAM, storage, network)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellhw
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellhw
prints a colour-coded hardware report: CPU, GPU, motherboard and BIOS, memory
modules, storage, network interfaces, fans, and battery status.
.PP
Memory details come from
.BR dmidecode (8)
when available (module count, total size, type, speed, form factor, part
number) and fall back to
.BR decode-dimms (1)
from i2c-tools. The raw JEDEC JEP106 manufacturer code reported by dmidecode
(e.g. \fB8313\fR) is resolved to the vendor name (e.g. \fBGolden Empire\fR)
using the table shipped as \fI/usr/share/wellutils/jedec.sh\fR.
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the report is drawn as boxes; when piped a plain
layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR: \fI~/.config/wellutils/lang.conf\fR,
then locale).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON on stdout; errors still go to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.TP
.B LANG / LC_MESSAGES
Locale used to pick the default language.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/wellutils/lang.sh
Translation table.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wellutils/box.sh
Adaptive box-drawing engine.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wellutils/jedec.sh
JEDEC JEP106 manufacturer ID table (data from i2c-tools, GPL-2.0).
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1),
.BR wellmem (1),
.BR decode-dimms (1),
.BR dmidecode (8)
